    "narrative": "The Austin Waves head into today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56), **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.39), and **Kyle Tucker** (71.13) anchoring our lineup. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our premier start, capitalizing on a soft matchup against Pecko (xERA 5.95) and a high-leverage spot in the three-hole, while **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a must-start despite a modest platoon drag because his raw power profile against Lugo, S is too significant to ignore. **Kyle Tucker** rounds out our top trio, providing the efficiency we covet; even with a slightly higher xERA for his opponent, his base projections remain elite, and he continues to be the primary engine for our category consistency.\n\nWe are navigating several high-difficulty matchups today, most notably for **Jackson Merrill** (49.36) and **Sam Antonacci** (43.59), who both face the formidable Paul Skenes and Jacob deGrom, respectively. **Jackson Merrill** holds a marginal score, but his elite sprint speed remains a priority for our strategy, making him a volatile but necessary play. The tightest decision on our roster involved **Miguel Vargas** (39.33), who was the first cut from the active lineup. While **Miguel Vargas** showed strong underlying metrics including a quality xwOBA, the optimizer ultimately pivoted toward the defensive stability and lineup positioning of our active starters, specifically penalizing **Miguel Vargas** for the difficulty of the Jacob deGrom assignment. \n\nInvestors should note the volatility surrounding our \"Lineup Pending\" players, specifically **Tommy White**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Sam Antonacci**. We have factored in the risk of facing elite arms like Skenes and deGrom; these matchups suppressed the scores of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Drake Baldwin** as well. We are monitoring the weather closely, though the primary risk today remains the structural challenge of facing top-tier starting pitching. We are also tracking the progress of **An